course: dictionary
lesson: 14
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples are the first peoples of their lands» uses Aboriginal as a name for the first peoples of Australia. The words around it, «first peoples», are the clue.
explain: Look at the capital letter too. Aboriginal with a capital A names the first peoples of Australia, like a proper name. Lower case aboriginal means belonging to a place from the very beginning, as in «aboriginal peoples of Canada». «Aboriginal art» and «Aboriginal culture» both use the capital letter.
explain: Say «Aboriginal people» or «Aboriginal peoples» today, not «an Aboriginal». When you meet a word about people, check the context and use the respectful wording you see in the text. «Though Aboriginal people had lived there for over 50,000 years» shows the clue: for over a long time means they were there first.
fact: Aboriginal (capital A) means belonging to the first peoples of Australia, who have lived there for tens of thousands of years.
fact: Aboriginal (lower case) means belonging to a place from the very beginning; native or original.
fact: Common phrases include «Aboriginal art», «Aboriginal culture» and «Acknowledgement of Country», a respectful statement at the start of events.
fact: In Canada, Aboriginal was used for First Nations, Inuit and Métis peoples, though Indigenous is more common now.
exercise: In «Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples», what does Aboriginal mean? | A modern city | A kind of boat | A sweet food | *Belonging to the first peoples of Australia
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Cook landed at Botany Bay, though Aboriginal people had lived there for over 50,000 years» that shows who lived there first. | Cook | Britain | *Aboriginal | Botany
exercise: Which sentence uses the capital letter correctly? | We learn about ABORIGINAL art in class. | *We learn about Aboriginal art in class. | We learn about aboriginal Art in class. | We learn about aboriginal art in class.
test: Which word means the same as lower case aboriginal, meaning native from the very beginning? | Newly arrived | *Native | Foreign | Modern
test: Which is the respectful way to talk about people today? | The aboriginals | An Aboriginal | Aboriginal man | *Aboriginal people
exam: Read «Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples are the first peoples of their lands, and their cultures deserve respect.» What does «first peoples» suggest? | The tallest people | The people who arrived last | *The people who lived in the land before anyone else | The people who sail ships
